<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Colombia</h1><p class="st-meta">1886 CE – present · capital Bogotá</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The centralised Colombian republic founded by the constitution of 1886, which lost Panama, endured decades of internal conflict and made peace with the FARC in 2016.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Liberal federation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-states-of-colombia">United States of Colombia</a> failed, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-nunez">Rafael Núñez</a> and the Conservatives imposed the constitution of 1886, which created a centralised <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gran-colombia">Republic of Colombia</a>, gave the president strong powers and restored the Catholic Church's role in education.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thousand-days-war">Thousand Days' War</a> of 1899 to 1902 devastated the country, and in 1903 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a> seceded with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> support. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">Coffee</a> became the main export. The assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorge-eliecer-gaitan">Jorge Eliécer Gaitán</a> in 1948 unleashed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-violencia">La Violencia</a>, a civil conflict ended by the power-sharing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-front-colombia">National Front</a> from 1958 to 1974. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">Guerrilla</a> groups such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolutionary-armed-forces-of-colombia">FARC</a>, founded in 1964, and drug cartels such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-escobar">Pablo Escobar's</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medellin">Medellín</a> fuelled violence for decades.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>A new constitution in 1991 replaced that of 1886. President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-santos">Juan Manuel Santos</a> signed a peace agreement with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolutionary-armed-forces-of-colombia">FARC</a> in 2016, winning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavo-petro">Gustavo Petro</a> became the first left-wing president in 2022.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-colombia.jpg" alt="Republic of Colombia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Colombia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1886 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bogotá</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rafael Núñez, Álvaro Uribe, Juan Manuel Santos</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/colombia">Colombia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Colombia, República de Colombia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1956&amp;focus=republic-of-colombia" aria-label="Republic of Colombia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2625 2005 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Colombia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2945 2261L2945 2261M2945 2261L2804 2099"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2945 2261h0M2804 2099h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2945 2261h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2945 2261h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bogotá. <a href="/atlas?year=1956&amp;focus=republic-of-colombia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
